## Tool Name: run_smbclient
### Description: Run smbclient to connect to an SMB/CIFS server and optionally execute commands.
Operations include things like getting files from the server to the local machine, putting files from the local machine to the server, retrieving directory information from the server and so on.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'target': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The target IP address or NetBIOS name.'}, 'service': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The name of the SMB service to connect to (e.g. the name of a share or a printer).'}, 'username': {'default': 'guest', 'type': 'string', 'description': 'The username for authentication. If not provided, defaults to "guest".'}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'The password required to access the specified service on the specified server. If not provided, no password will be used (\'-N\' for anonymous access). If empty string "", forces an empty password via \'user%\'. If a string is provided, uses that password.'}, 'command': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': 'ls', 'description': 'Semicolon-separated list of commands to be executed.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Additional arguments for smbclient (e.g. '-p 139')."}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum time in seconds that the command is allowed to run for (default is 120 seconds).'}}, 'required': ['target', 'service'], 'type': 'object'}```

